From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdio: add quirk for broken CCCR revision

The RTL8192ES fitted to the ZTE MF283V consistently returns 0x34 from
SDIO_CCCR_CCCR.  The low nibble formally selects CCCR/FBR format 4.00,
but this device otherwise behaves as an older SDIO 2.00 card and works
with the existing format 3.00 register parser.

Do not enable format 4.00 globally without implementing and testing it.
Instead, describe the affected device variant in the devicetree and apply
an early quirk before the CCCR is parsed.  For that device only, treat the
exact value 0x34 as format 3.00.  Continue to reject revision 4 on all
other cards and reject every other unsupported value on the affected card.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h                     |  3 ++
 drivers/mmc/core/sdio.c                       |  2 +
 include/linux/mmc/card.h                      |  1 +
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/quirks.h
@@ -212,6 +212,9 @@ static const struct mmc_fixup __maybe_un
 };
 
 static const struct mmc_fixup __maybe_unused sdio_card_init_methods[] = {
+	SDIO_FIXUP_COMPATIBLE("zte,mf283v-rtl8192es", add_quirk,
+			      MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_CCCR_REV),
+
 	SDIO_FIXUP_COMPATIBLE("ti,wl1251", wl1251_quirk, 0),
 
 	SDIO_FIXUP_COMPATIBLE("silabs,wf200", add_quirk,
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/sdio.c
@@ -154,6 +154,8 @@ static int sdio_read_cccr(struct mmc_car
 		goto out;
 
 	cccr_vsn = data & 0x0f;
+	if ((card->quirks & MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_CCCR_REV) && data == 0x34)
+		cccr_vsn = SDIO_CCCR_REV_3_00;
 
 	if (cccr_vsn > SDIO_CCCR_REV_3_00) {
 		pr_err("%s: unrecognised CCCR structure version %d\n",
--- a/include/linux/mmc/card.h
+++ b/include/linux/mmc/card.h
@@ -332,6 +332,7 @@ struct mmc_card {
 #define MMC_QUIRK_NO_UHS_DDR50_TUNING	(1<<18) /* Disable DDR50 tuning */
 #define MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_MDT    (1<<19) /* Wrong manufacturing year */
 #define MMC_QUIRK_FIXED_SECURE_ERASE_TRIM_TIME	(1<<20) /* Secure erase/trim time is fixed regardless of size */
+#define MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_CCCR_REV	(1<<21) /* Incorrect CCCR revision */
 
 	bool			written_flag;	/* Indicates eMMC has been written since power on */
 	bool			reenable_cmdq;	/* Re-enable Command Queue */
